    ],
    "lyrics": {
      "text": "By the in-ter-ces-sions of Thy Mar-tyrs, O Lord, grant rest un-to the souls of Thy ser-vants.\n\nThe ho-ly Mar-tyrs were of-fered up un-to God the glo-ri-ous as a most sa-cred and___ whole-burnt of-fer-ing and the ho-ly first-fruits of all the na-ture of man, for ev-er af-ter grant-ing sal-va-tion un-to__ us.__\n\nTheir souls shall dwell a-mong good__ things.\n\nThat bless-ed heav-en-ly life on high and a por-tion of Thy gifts of grace do Thou, O Mas---ter, vouch-safe to give to Thy faith-ful ser-vants be-fore us fall-en a-sleep, and grant them full re-demp-tion from all their tres-pass--es.__\n\nGlo-ry to the Fa-ther, and to the Son, and to the Ho--ly Spir-it.\n\nA-lone by na-ture cre-at-ing life, Thou Who art the Sea of Good-ness in-fi-nite in depth___ and un-trace-a-ble, count those who have died wor-thy of Thy King-dom on high, O on-ly Lord Im-mor-tal and all-com-pas-sion--ate.__\n\nBoth now and ev--er, and un-to the ag--es of ag-es. A-men.\n\nHe that was born of thee is be-come the strength, and the song, and the sal-va-tion of all them___ that once had been lost, from the gates of Ha-des de-liv-’ring them that with faith do call thee blest, O thou Sov-’reign La-dy of the__ world.__"
    }
